│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_steiner_broadcast                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the greedy shortest-path tree expansion with an exact directed Steiner-tree       │
│                          │ dynamic program for practical destination counts. The prior algorithm chooses the next    │
│                          │ cheapest attachment locally, which can commit to expensive relay choices and miss a       │
│                          │ slightly more expensive shared relay that substantially reduces subsequent destination    │
│                          │ costs.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new algorithm computes the minimum-cost directed subnetwork rooted at `src` that      │
│                          │ reaches all requested destinations. Its dynamic program considers both merging            │
│                          │ independent destination subtrees at a relay and routing from upstream nodes into those    │
│                          │ shared subtrees. This explicitly rewards shared links, avoids redundant source transfers, │
│                          │ and finds lower-cost multi-cloud broadcast topologies. For unusually large destination    │
│                          │ sets, it retains a bounded greedy fallback to avoid exponential planning cost.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
