│ patch_name               │ shared_broadcast_tree                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a greedy shared broadcast-tree    │
│                          │ construction. The previous approach optimizes each destination in isolation, which can    │
│                          │ repeatedly transfer the same partitions over expensive upstream links. The new approach   │
│                          │ grows a multicast tree from the source: at each step it connects the nearest remaining    │
│                          │ destination to any node already receiving the broadcast. This minimizes each incremental  │
│                          │ network cost, naturally reuses existing low-cost links, and can satisfy destinations      │
│                          │ encountered as intermediate nodes without creating redundant transfers.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each partition follows the resulting tree path, preserving the existing                   │
│                          │ `BroadCastTopology` representation while allowing downstream topology consumers to        │
│                          │ recognize shared edges as overlapping broadcast transfers.                                │
