│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ relay_bundle_fallback                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the large-fan-out fallback where exact Steiner dynamic programming is          │
│                          │ intentionally avoided. The previous greedy method connects only one destination at a      │
│                          │ time, so it can miss a cheap relay that accepts one ingress transfer and then fans out to │
│                          │ several destinations. This edit precomputes low-cost relay-to-destination paths and, at   │
│                          │ every iteration, evaluates both single-destination and two-destination relay bundles.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Candidates are scored by incremental union-edge cost per newly served destination.        │
│                          │ Existing tree edges have zero marginal cost, so the heuristic explicitly prefers paths    │
│                          │ that overlap previously installed transfers. Pair bundles model parallel fan-out from a   │
│                          │ relay and avoid paying redundant ingress links separately for destinations that can share │
│                          │ them. The resulting selected graph remains rooted at the source, and the existing output  │
│                          │ logic continues to assign the shared routes to every partition.                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
