│ patch_name               │ exact_steiner_broadcast                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the nearest-reached-node greedy attachment with an exact directed Steiner dynamic │
│                          │ program for broadcast-sized destination sets. The dynamic program jointly selects relay   │
│                          │ paths and branch points, charging each selected network edge once regardless of how many  │
│                          │ destinations reuse it. This avoids greedy choices that can prevent later destinations     │
│                          │ from sharing an inexpensive trunk.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For every subset of destinations and candidate relay node, the algorithm computes the     │
│                          │ minimum cost needed to broadcast from that node to the subset. It combines independently  │
│                          │ served subsets at a relay and relaxes those relay solutions backward across the directed  │
│                          │ network. The resulting root state is an optimal shared directed broadcast topology under  │
│                          │ additive edge costs. The topology is then expanded into root-to-destination paths for     │
│                          │ every partition, preserving shared prefixes for overlapping transfers.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
