│                          │ planner uses a directed Steiner dynamic program for small-to-medium destination sets,     │
│                          │ which finds a minimum shared-edge broadcast tree rather than relying on greedy attachment │
│                          │ order. For larger terminal sets, it falls back to a marginal-cost shared-tree heuristic   │
│                          │ to retain practical runtime. Shared tree prefixes are emitted identically for every       │
│                          │ partition, allowing downstream scheduling to transfer each partition once and fan it out  │
│                          │ across destinations.                                                                      │
