╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ terminal_aware_multicast_growth                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the nearest-destination multicast-tree growth rule with a terminal-aware          │
│                          │ shared-path rule. The existing algorithm selects the lowest-cost connector to one         │
│                          │ destination, even when a slightly more expensive connector would traverse and satisfy     │
│                          │ several remaining destinations. This can create unnecessary branches and duplicate        │
│                          │ upstream transfers.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The revised selection evaluates every currently reachable destination connector and       │
│                          │ scores it by marginal network cost per newly covered destination on that connector. It    │
│                          │ therefore favors low-cost trunk paths that deliver the broadcast to multiple clouds       │
│                          │ before branching, while still using `multi_source_dijkstra` to attach each new route at   │
│                          │ the cheapest already-receiving node. Marginal edge cost is calculated only for edges not  │
│                          │ already present in the multicast tree, preventing shared edges from being charged again   │
│                          │ during route selection. Deterministic tie-breaking preserves reproducible topologies.     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0285                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ gpt-5.6-terra                                                                             │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'low', 'summary': 'auto'}                                                      │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 21; deleted: 0; modified: 8;                                                       │
