│ patch_description        │ This version plans shared broadcast routes as a directed Steiner arborescence rather than │
│                          │ independently routing each destination.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For modest destination sets, it uses an exact dynamic-programming directed Steiner        │
│                          │ solver. The solver explicitly evaluates shared prefixes and branching points, producing   │
│                          │ the minimum-cost union of network links required to reach all destinations. For larger    │
│                          │ sets, it uses a hybrid strategy: solve a high-cost/far-away core exactly, then attach     │
│                          │ remaining destinations through marginal shortest paths where already selected broadcast   │
│                          │ edges have zero incremental cost. A pure marginal-attachment candidate is also evaluated, │
│                          │ and the lower-cost route union is selected.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned `BroadCastTopology` format remains unchanged: every destination and          │
│                          │ partition receives a source-to-destination edge list, while shared physical edges are     │
│                          │ reused across destination routes.                                                         │
