│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_steiner_core                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the purely greedy multicast expansion with an exact directed Steiner-tree dynamic │
│                          │ program for small destination sets. The current Prim-like strategy commits early to the   │
│                          │ nearest terminal, which can prevent discovery of a slightly more expensive relay branch   │
│                          │ that substantially reduces total shared-link cost for later destinations.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement computes the minimum-cost shared directed subgraph connecting the source  │
│                          │ to every reachable destination when there are at most nine terminals. It combines         │
│                          │ terminal subsets at relay nodes and relaxes those shared subtrees backward across the     │
│                          │ network, thereby explicitly valuing overlapping transfers. For larger terminal sets, it   │
│                          │ preserves the existing scalable greedy behavior. This hybrid keeps runtime bounded while  │
│                          │ improving the cases where exact shared branching is most beneficial.                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
