│ patch_description        │ This version combines the reliable graph sanitization and shared-tree approach from the   │
│                          │ current implementation with the simple shortest-path behavior of the crossover program.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It improves broadcast cost by:                                                            │
│                          │ - Computing an exact directed Steiner broadcast tree for up to 11 destinations, allowing  │
│                          │ common relay links to be paid for once.                                                   │
│                          │ - Falling back to a scalable marginal-cost multi-source expansion for larger destination  │
│                          │ sets.                                                                                     │
│                          │ - Removing invalid, negative, NaN, inbound-source, and self-loop links before routing.    │
│                          │ - Normalizing selected links into source-reachable shortest paths, eliminating            │
│                          │ unnecessary links and cycles while preserving delivery to every reachable destination.    │
│                          │ - Maintaining the original `BroadCastTopology` output format: every destination/partition │
│                          │ receives its own edge-list path.                                                          │
