│ patch_name               │ cost_aware_tree_materialization                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The dynamic program reconstructs a minimum-cost shared edge union, but the final          │
│                          │ per-destination routes are currently extracted with an unweighted shortest-path search.   │
│                          │ If reconstruction produces multiple source-to-destination routes within the shared union, │
│                          │ NetworkX selects the route with the fewest hops rather than the cheapest transfer route.  │
│                          │ This can materialize unnecessarily expensive cloud egress links and can prevent redundant │
│                          │ expensive branches from being omitted by the topology consumer.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Use cost-weighted path extraction when materializing destination routes. The selected     │
│                          │ path remains entirely inside the optimized shared broadcast union, preserves source       │
│                          │ reachability, and minimizes each destination's transfer cost among the available shared   │
│                          │ routes.                                                                                   │
