│ patch_name               │ incumbent_pruned_steiner                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Construct the scalable shared-tree solution first and use its unique-link cost as an      │
│                          │ incumbent upper bound for the exact directed Steiner solver. Because all valid transfer   │
│                          │ costs are non-negative, no DP subtree whose cost already reaches the incumbent can        │
│                          │ contribute to a cheaper final broadcast tree. This safely prunes merge and                │
│                          │ reverse-relaxation states, allowing the exact solver to cover twelve destinations rather  │
│                          │ than eleven while retaining the greedy topology whenever exact search cannot improve it.  │
│                          │ This increases opportunities to find lower-cost shared relay trees on larger multi-cloud  │
│                          │ broadcasts without sacrificing a known feasible solution.                                 │
