│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ incumbent_pruned_steiner                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Construct a feasible shared broadcast tree with a marginal-cost planner before running    │
│                          │ the exact Dreyfus-Wagner dynamic program. Its link-union cost is a valid upper bound on   │
│                          │ the optimal broadcast cost. Because all sanitized transfer costs are non-negative, any    │
│                          │ partial DP state whose cost is already at least this incumbent cannot contribute to a     │
│                          │ strictly cheaper complete topology, so it is safely discarded during subset merging and   │
│                          │ reverse shortest-path relaxation.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves exactness whenever the DP finds an improvement, while avoiding exponential │
│                          │ work on states that cannot beat the already feasible broadcast. If the incumbent is       │
│                          │ optimal, the solver directly returns it after proving no strictly cheaper state exists.   │
│                          │ This is especially valuable for larger multi-cloud fan-out sets where redundant state     │
│                          │ exploration otherwise dominates runtime.                                                  │
